## What to deliver

Author the muzzle-blast system operation by operation — the big blast core, the
forward gout of flame and heavy embers, and the thick rolling smoke plume (as timed
bursts at the shot instant), with the forces and per-particle curves that make them
project forward, arc, and roll as the brief describes, and the timeline kept
**one-shot** — running `particle-3d render` to simulate and check the effect as you
go. When the simulated `effect.gif` reads as a single heavy-cannon muzzle blast that
decays cleanly to empty, run `render` one last time and stop: the recorded
`actions.json` (and the `system.json` it emits) is your finished submission.
